---
import CommercialLayout from '../layouts/CommercialLayout.astro';
import proof from '../data/workflowProof.json';
---

<CommercialLayout
  title="Synthetic workflow proof"
  description="A plainly labeled local-fixture proof showing durable intake, duplicate handling, malformed input rejection, and downstream recovery evidence."
>
  <header class="page-intro">
    <div class="commercial-shell page-intro__grid">
      <div>
        <h1 class="commercial-title">
          Synthetic proof, with its limits attached.
        </h1>
        <p>
          This rehearsal uses invented data against the local intake fixture. It
          is not a client result, availability claim, external-provider test, or
          live production monitor.
        </p>
      </div>
      <p class="page-intro__note">
        Evidence class<br /><strong>Studio-owned synthetic demonstration</strong
        ><br />
        Schema {proof.schema} · {proof.runtime_claim.replaceAll('_', ' ')}<br />
        Generated {new Date(proof.generated_at).toISOString()}
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="commercial-section commercial-section--ink">
    <div class="commercial-shell">
      <div class="offer-ledger">
        <div class="offer-row">
          <h2>Durable intake</h2><p class="offer-price">
            HTTP {proof.intake.success.status}
          </p><p>
            <code>{proof.intake.success.reference}</code> was returned only after
            the synthetic record committed.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="offer-row">
          <h2>Idempotent retry</h2><p class="offer-price">
            HTTP {proof.intake.duplicate.status}
          </p><p>
            <code>duplicate: {String(proof.intake.duplicate.duplicate)}</code> and
            <code
              >same_reference: {
                String(proof.intake.duplicate.same_reference)
              }</code
            >. The retry did not create a second record.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="offer-row">
          <h2>Malformed input</h2><p class="offer-price">
            HTTP {proof.intake.malformed.status}
          </p><p>
            The fixture returned <code>{proof.intake.malformed.error}</code> and did
            not produce a success receipt.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="offer-row">
          <h2>Notification retry</h2><p class="offer-price">
            retry {proof.notification.injected_failure.retry_count}
          </p><p>
            <code>{proof.notification.injected_failure.code}</code> failed once. The
            <code>{proof.notification.recovery.adapter}</code> fixture later delivered
            <code>{proof.notification.recovery.sent_count}</code> queued notifications.
            No external provider was called.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="offer-row">
          <h2>Workflow incident recovery</h2><p class="offer-price">
            {proof.workflow.status_sequence.join(' → ')}
          </p><p>
            A <code>{proof.workflow.check_adapter}</code> check opened an incident
            when loopback HTTP was unavailable. A later HTTP commit matched the durable
            database record and recovered that same incident. Evidence references:
            <code>{proof.workflow.evidence_refs.join(', ')}</code>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="commercial-section">
    <div class="commercial-shell">
      <div class="commercial-section__head">
        <h2>What this rehearsal proves—and what it does not.</h2>
        <p class="commercial-section__intro">
          The published values come from the regenerated local fixture artifact.
          They demonstrate the intake and recovery mechanism with owned
          synthetic data; they do not establish production availability or
          third-party delivery.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="boundary-list">
        <div>
          <h3>Exercised</h3><p>
            Durable commit, an idempotent retry, malformed input rejection, one
            injected notification failure with owned-file retry, and recovery of
            one workflow-check incident through the loopback HTTP and durable
            database path.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Limitations</h3><ul>
            {proof.limitations.map((limitation) => <li>{limitation}</li>)}
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p>
        <a href="/proofs/workflow/synthetic-proof.json"
          >Download the sanitized JSON evidence</a
        >
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/proofs/">See the existing proof archive</a> · <a
          href="/case-studies/">Read provenance-labeled field notes</a
        > · <a href="/portfolio/">Browse reference work and sample outputs</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</CommercialLayout>
